      "verification": "Three durable follow-up records created, each a fast_follow_of decideWorkflowHibernation, verified present via adv_change_list (total 58 -> 60 with investigateOrphanWorkflow already counted, confirming exactly 3 created and no duplicates):\n\n1. investigateOrphanWorkflow (DEC-4) — capability advance-workflow. Carries established facts (scanner healthy, historyScannerEnabled defaults true, ADV only terminates at 5 cited call sites), the unestablished mechanism, and the mandatory DDC4 opening constraint requiring an explicit population predicate.\n2. addEpicClosePath (DEC-3) — capability advance-epics. 40 running epic workflows, zero ever closed; completion machinery exists at workflows.ts:2494-2522 but nothing drives it. Explicitly framed as correctness/shape, not storage (epic history is only ~1.2 MB).\n3. addSignalLossObservability (DEC-5 / rq-hib04) — capability advance-workflow. Carries DDC3 observability-only bounds, the signal/query-only surface law, and the ADR-0003 no-throw rule.\n\nEach record states its scope, evidence anchors, and governing constraint, so it can be started cold.\n\nConstraint compliance: C1 — records only, nothing implemented. OOS4 — orphan reclamation explicitly deferred until the mechanism is known. OOS3 — no per-session task-queue work folded in. DONT3 — these are distinct downstream items ADR-002 names as consequences, not per-symptom tickets substituting for a verdict; the verdict is made and recorded.\n\nNote: all three adv_change_create calls returned ToolExecutionTimeout at 10000ms, but every write landed. The timeout is a post-write readback hang, not a write failure — verified by listing before any retry, so no duplicates were created.",
