      "topic": "Design validation — Workflow Hibernation Lifecycle (ADR-002)",
      "sources": [
        {
          "label": "Temporal continue-as-new design pattern",
          "locator": "https://docs.temporal.io/design-patterns/continue-as-new",
          "summary": "Authoritative: 'Forgetting to drain Signals before continuing. Any Signals received but not yet processed are lost when Continue-As-New starts a fresh execution.' Continue-as-new does NOT automatically preserve pending signals; author must drain and carry as args."
        },
        {
          "label": "Temporal TS SDK — message passing / allHandlersFinished",
          "locator": "https://docs.temporal.io/develop/typescript/workflows/message-passing",
          "summary": "Guidance is to wait for allHandlersFinished before continue-as-new; signals processed by handlers, not auto-serialized to next run. Completion and continue-as-new share this drain requirement."
        },
        {
          "label": "Temporal community — TS SDK signals and continueAsNew",
          "locator": "https://community.temporal.io/t/ts-sdk-signals-and-continueasnew/4406",
          "summary": "Maintainer confirms at high signal rates 'the application has to be remodeled' and signals must be carried manually to the next run. Confirms no automatic carry-over."
        },
        {
          "label": "Temporal TS SDK source — setDefaultSignalHandler",
          "locator": "https://github.com/temporalio/sdk-typescript/blob/main/packages/workflow/src/workflow.ts",
          "summary": "setDefaultSignalHandler calls activator.dispatchBufferedSignals() — dispatch is WITHIN the same run, not a carry to the next run. Confirms unregistered-signal discard is not solved by continue-as-new."
        },
        {
          "label": "Temporal entity-workflow pattern",
          "locator": "https://docs.temporal.io/design-patterns/entity-workflow",
          "summary": "Entity workflows run for entity lifetime, use continue-as-new for longevity, complete only on entity deletion/terminal. No guidance recommends completing idle live entities to bound running count. Supports design claim #4."
        },
        {
          "label": "Temporal entity loyalty-points guide",
          "locator": "https://docs.temporal.io/guides/entity-pattern-loyalty-points",
          "summary": "'Unprocessed Signals are preserved' is achieved by the workflow MANUALLY serializing them into state passed to continue_as_new — not automatic SDK behavior. Confirms claim #3 misattributes the mechanism."
        },
        {
          "label": "Temporal control-plane blog (entity workflow)",
          "locator": "https://temporal.io/blog/how-to-build-a-resilient-platform-control-plane-with-temporal",
          "summary": "Entity workflow = durable control-plane record for a resource; continue-as-new prevents unbounded history. Reinforces workflow-lifetime-mirrors-entity-lifetime as canonical."
        },
        {
          "label": "Temporal GitHub issue #2860 — RequestCancel on completed returns OK",
          "locator": "https://github.com/temporalio/temporal/issues/2860",
