        "recommendation": "Proceed toward ADR approval AFTER restating shape argument #3. The NEGATIVE verdict is correct and well-supported by Temporal's canonical entity-workflow pattern plus four independent shape arguments; it should not be overturned. But claim #3's assertion that continue-as-new 'serializes pending signals into the next run' and is 'strictly safer' on signal grounds is refuted by Temporal docs and by ADV's own workflows.ts:2285-2288. Restate to the liveness framing (no spec amendment needed, fully in-scope edit to design.md, the change's deliverable). Spec-law is otherwise clear and C2/C3 are satisfied; alternatives are acceptably disposed. required_validation_consistency = caution only because of the claim #3 restatement; no other blockers."
      },
      "recommendation": "Proceed toward ADR-002 approval AFTER restating shape argument #3 to the liveness framing. The NEGATIVE verdict is architecturally sound: four independent shape arguments (#1 entity-mirror-correct, #2 cache-vs-mirror regression, #4 no Temporal guidance to complete idle entities — verified across docs.temporal.io/design-patterns/entity-workflow, the loyalty-points guide, and the control-plane blog, #5 real defect is entity-lifecycle discipline) justify it without claim #3. DEC-1's bundle-generation parity is verified correct at worker-bundle-manifest.ts:29,81-89 (signal-SET equality holds; DDC1/DDC2 add the needed re-verification caveats). DEC-2's self-completion-by-signal is the correct single-threaded arbiter and RequestCancel-returns-OK is confirmed (temporal #2860). Spec-law: no conflict — advance-delivery's signal/query-only law is respected (C2), DEC-4's established-vs-unestablished split satisfies C3, no spec requires a positive decision. The single caution is claim #3's false signal-preservation premise (violates DONT2, weakens AC3/SC2 precision): restate it to 'continue-as-new preserves entity LIVENESS, not signals; both paths drop undrained unregistered signals, which is exactly why DEC-5 is verdict-independent.' This small in-scope edit to design.md strengthens internal consistency. Alternatives acceptably disposed; multi-namespace split is the only omission and is fairly deferred to the revisit trigger.",
